  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amazon Web Services has $401M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Amazon Web Services received 98 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.1M. Obligations rose year over year, up 27.6% compared with the prior year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $322M obligated, followed by the General Services Administration with $28.8M and the Department of Energy with $22M. Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services is the largest market for Amazon Web Services with $382M obligated. Other material markets include Computer Systems Design Services with $19M and Custom Computer Programming Services with $261K. Historical obligations show steady growth from FY21 through FY26, with FY21 at $39.2M, FY22 at $27.3M, FY23 at $98.6M, FY24 at $246M, FY25 at $314M, and FY26 at $401M. The mix of large DoD obligations and heavy emphasis on computing infrastructure signals that Amazon Web Services remains a central cloud and hosting supplier to the federal government this fiscal year.",
